<sn><md>### Vitamin A

#### Sources

+++ view dietary source of vitaminA
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/dietary_sources_of_vitaminA.png)
+++

* **Animal Sources:** Eggs, cow's milk, butter, cheese, yogurt, liver, and fatty fish (such as cod).
* **Plant Sources:** Foods rich in `carotene`, including red amaranthus, arum leaves (*kachu shak*), stem amaranth (*data shak*), basil, jute leaves, water spinach (*kalmi shak*), mint, peas, carrots, lady finger, cabbage, peanuts, and fruits like `mango, ripe papaya, and jackfruit`. `Carrots` are particularly rich in this nutrient.

#### Functions:

1. Facilitates overall bodily `growth and development`.
2. Preserves `epithelial tissue` function in skin and corneas.
3. Promotes healthy `teeth, gums, and bones`.
4. Maintains `visual acuity` and prevents `night blindness`.
5. Strengthens `defense` against infectious illnesses.

#### Deficiency &amp; Excess Symptoms:
* **Xerophthalmia:** Starts as `night blindness` and can progress to corneal ulceration or complete blindness if unmanaged.
* **Other Symptoms:** Susceptibility to `colds, sore throats, coughs, skin lesions` (small bumps around hair follicles), and urinary issues.
* Excessive consumption can be `toxic`.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Vitamin D

+++ view
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/sources_of_vitaminD.png)
+++

* **Synthesis &amp; Sources:** `Synthesized in the skin` via UV light exposure, converting `cholesterol into active` forms through the liver and kidneys. Key dietary sources include `egg yolk, milk, butter, cabbage, liver, and oily fish`.
* **Functions:** Enhances `calcium absorption` necessary for bone building.
* **Deficiency &amp; Excess Symptoms:**
* Deficiency leads to `rickets in children`.
* Excessive intake causes `hyperabsorption of calcium and phosphorus`, leading to dangerous `calcification in the kidneys, heart, and blood vessels`.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Vitamin E

* **Sources:** `Plant oils` (especially palm oil, corn oil, cottonseed oil, sunflower oil) and `lettuce` leaves.
* **Functions:** Acts as an `antioxidant`, helping prevent `arterial fat accumulation` and keeping skin healthy.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Vitamin B Complex

Comprising `12 distinct water-soluble` vitamins, this group is essential for `brain health, nervous system activity, cellular metabolism, and reproductive processes`.

+++ view
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/sources_of_vitaminsB.png)
+++

| Vitamin | Primary Sources | Key Deficiency Symptoms |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Thiamin (B₁)** | **Plant:** Husked rice, flour, pulses, oilseeds, nuts, fresh fruits, vegetables. <br> **Animal:** Liver, egg, milk, fish. | Beriberi, nerve weakness, depression, fatigue, loss of appetite, weight loss. |
| **Riboflavin (B₂)** | Liver, egg, milk, green vegetables, young plant shoots, sprouted seeds. | Cracks at the corners of the mouth, oral/tongue sores, rough skin. |
| **Niacin / Nicotinic Acid (B₃)** * | Meat, liver, flour (*ata*), pulses, nuts, oilseeds, chickpeas, vegetables. | Pellagra (characterized by the 3 Ds: dermatitis, diarrhea, and dementia). |
| **Pyridoxine (B₆)** | Rice, flour (*ata*), fish, meat, vegetables, chickpeas, fungi, kidney, egg yolk. | Loss of appetite, nausea/vomiting, anemia. |
| **Cobalamin / Cyanocobalamin (B₁₂)** | Liver, milk, fish, meat, egg, cheese, kidney. | Anemia, nervous system disorders. |


</md></sn><sn><md>### Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid)

+++ view
![img](https://i.pinimg.com/736x/07/54/7b/07547b215ad57bdac96c64ab6f6fe584.jpg)
+++

* **Sources:**
* **Fruits:** Indian gooseberry (*amloki*), lemon, orange, tomato, pineapple, guava.
* **Vegetables:** Radish, lettuce, coriander leaves, mint, green chili, cauliflower, bitter gourd.
* *Note: Dried fruits, seeds, and canned foods generally lack Vitamin C.*


* **Functions:**
1. `Strengthens cells` in skin, bones, and teeth.
2. Assists `tissue repair and wound healing`.
3. Aids fat, protein, and amino acid `metabolism.`
4. Keeps `skin smooth and bright` while enhancing immune function.

+++ view
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/deficiency_of_vitaminC.png)
+++

* **Deficiency Symptoms:**
* `Scurvy` (bleeding and swollen gums, loose teeth).
* Impaired bone density, skin sores, slow wound healing, reduced immunity, and frequent colds.</md></sn>